    "rationale": "Regional isolation probes reduced the affected regions from the 440-485 ms starting p95 range to 315-326 ms while leaving other regions materially unchanged, showing that cross-region propagation participates in the regression. Resetting retry state at every cross-region boundary reduced all-region p95 to 215-235 ms and mean retries to 0.9-1.1, directly supporting retained retry-state feedback. In contrast, doubling service capacity left all-region p95 at 420-455 ms and mean retries at 2.7-3.1, so capacity saturation is not the primary mechanism. This also addresses O2: load relief can lower latency without removing retry amplification, so its improvement is not causal identification. O3 further disfavors saturation, while O4 is consistent with cross-region retry feedback. The evidence therefore selects H_retry_feedback as the primary mechanism and rejects H_capacity as primary; H_clock_sync may contribute but need not be rejected by the public terminal contract."
  },
